==German==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|houwan}}.  Cognate with English {{term|hew}}.

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|haut|hieb|gehauen}}

# {{transitive|colloquial|lang=de}} to [[beat]]; to [[hit]] (someone); to [[spank]]
#: ''Ich '''hau''' dich gleich.'' — “Now I’m going to spank you.”
# {{reflexive|colloquial|of multiple people|lang=de}} to [[fight]]; to [[tangle]]
# {{transitive}} to [[chop]]; to chop down; to [[cut]]; to [[whittle]]; to [[hew]]

====Conjugation====
In casual speech, {{term|hauen}} is often conjugated like a weak verb, with the past tense {{term|haute}}, etc.
{{de-conj-old|haue|haust|haut|hieb, haute|gehauen|hiebe, haute|hau|haut|haben}}

